ursor-pointer hover:bg-blue-50 rounded\\\">masalalarini</span> <span class=\\\"cursor-pointer hover:bg-blue-50 rounded\\\">qamrab</span> <span class=\\\"cursor-pointer hover:bg-blue-50 rounded\\\">oladi.</span></p>\",\"ru\":\"<p class=\\\"docData;DOCY;v5;3827;\\\">Until October 2023, Sanjar Valiev served in the Department of External Relations of the Presidential Administration of the Republic of Uzbekistan, where he was engaged in a broad range of policy-related responsibilities.</p><p>Over many years, Valiev advanced his expertise in foreign policy and international security issues at the Institute for Strategic and Regional Studies and other leading national think tanks, contributing to high-level analytical work and policy development.</p><p>His areas of professional interest include international relations, sustainable development, and global and regional security.</p>\",\"en\":\"<p class=\\\"docData;DOCY;v5;3827;\\\">Until October 2023, Sanjar Valiev served in the Department of External Relations of the Presidential Administration of the Republic of Uzbekistan, where he was engaged in a broad range of policy-related responsibilities.</p><p>Over many years, Valiev advanced his expertise in foreign policy and international security issues at the Institute for Strategic and Regional Studies and other leading national think tanks, contributing to high-level analytical work and policy development.</p><p>His areas of professional interest include international relations, sustainable development, and global and regional security.</p>\"}',0,4,'{\"uz\":\"\",\"ru\":\"\",\"en\":\"\"}','','','','','Rahbariyat'),
